  "body": "Implements the remaining issue #3322 audit-history scope (task 13199, lane code-x): the retention/archive/backup-restore remainder after PR #5137 (audit v2) and PR #5141 (ingestion).\n\n## What lands\n- **Archive-before-prune retention contract** (`pm-stack/aggregator/src/events.ts`): both retention bounds (30 days / 5000 records) now flow through one gate, `partitionRetention`. Records leaving the hot stream are first appended — deduplicated by stable id, in stored-chain order, with their original hashes — to monthly partitions under `events.json.archive/` (`events-archive-YYYY-MM.json`). If an archive write fails, pruning is deferred and `health()` reports it; a record is never dropped unarchived. A chain that fails verification is never laundered into the archive, and never-chained records drop only with a loud log.\n- **Archive integrity + visible gap**: `verifyArchivedRecords` recomputes every archived record's hash; partitions are re-verified before every merge-write. `health()` gains `archivedRecords`, an `archive` verdict, and `historyGap` — when the hot chain's retention anchor names a pruned predecessor no partition holds (pre-contract pruning, a lost partition), the gap is a named field, not a silent hole.\n- **Backup set** (`nixos/home/pm-dashboard-backup.sh`): every generation now stages and manifest-records `aggregator/events.json.outbox.jsonl` (when present), the `aggregator/events.json.archive/` tree, and `aggregator/activity-ingestion.json`, alongside the already-required `events.json`. No #1514 database-backup duplication.\n- **Docs**: `pm-stack/aggregator/docs/audit-event-retention.md` — limits, integrity rules, backup set, and the restore procedure.\n\n## Restore evidence (new tests, `test/events-archive-3322.test.ts`)\n- Load-path pruning archives records byte-identical to what was stored; the archive verifies after a restart, with contiguous links from genesis.\n- Append past the bound is archived, not dropped; count and time bounds both split through `partitionRetention` with pruned = oldest, in stored order.\n- A tampered archive partition fails the archive health verdict; a pre-contract anchored chain reports `historyGap.present`.\n- Full round trip: a fixture state (hot events + archived history + a pending retry in the outbox + ingestion checkpoints/seen IDs) is copied into a manifest-verified generation (sha256 + size per file, all four audit members present), restored into an isolated dir, and shown to recover — outbox flushed with no duplicates, retained chain verifies, archived history intact and not duplicated into the hot stream, and replaying the same activity deliveries yields `ingested: 0, duplicates: 2` with the stream unchanged.\n\nIssue #3322 stays open per its own instruction (\"do not claim the overall #3322 issue complete until the audit-specific backup/restore evidence exists\") — this PR supplies that evidence for review; the queue task completes as pr_opened with the evidence attached.\n\nRefs #3322\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796729841&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7665&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7665&signature=68f8dd1d9237449e61f847609d067d2b657ee6e72b94f554ea37b8c347e7f73a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7665?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need